{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Fleetwood Mac and Hall & Oates feel like natural next choices because their melodic pop-rock connects with my listening to The Cars and classic-rock collections.",
    "Lesley Gore strongly matches the mid-'60s pop I explored with AM Gold, while Billy Joel fits my interest in memorable songs and artist compilations."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shania Twain's country-pop does not fit the older pop and classic rock I want right now, even though the greatest-hits format looks familiar.",
    "I cannot judge the collections titled only Greatest Hits or Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 without knowing the artist; the title alone gives me no musical reason to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections lean too heavily on my interest in greatest-hits albums, when the artist and musical style are what make those collections appealing.",
    "An interest in melodic pop seems to have been stretched too broadly: Manilow and Olivia Newton-John have some appeal, but I would choose the stronger classic-rock and '60s matches first."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to mid-'60s pop matters especially strongly to me, which is why Lesley Gore stands out beyond simply being another best-of collection.",
    "My history includes newer pop and a Christmas album, but those interests do not make every pop compilation equally appealing for my current listening mood."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar pop and rock collections, but sometimes treated the compilation format as a stronger match than the music itself."
}"}
